    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# 4.07 — Space Forms and Constant Curvature\n\nStage 2 built three geometries by hand: Euclidean, spherical and hyperbolic, each as a set with a transformation group in Klein's sense. Stage 4 has been building geometry from a metric instead. This notebook shows they are the same list — and that the list is complete.\n\n**Constant curvature.** $M$ has constant sectional curvature $K$ if $K(\\sigma) = K$ for every 2-plane $\\sigma$ at every point. Equivalently, the curvature tensor takes the form\n\n$$R_{ijkl} = K\\,(g_{ik}g_{jl} - g_{il}g_{jk}),$$\n\nthe only tensor with Riemann's symmetries built from $g$ alone.\n\n**Schur's lemma.** For $n \\ge 3$, if $K(\\sigma)$ is independent of $\\sigma$ at each point — *isotropy* — then it is automatically independent of the point too. Pointwise isotropy forces global homogeneity. The contracted Bianchi identity is what does it, and dimension 2 is excluded because there is only one plane per point, so every surface is trivially isotropic.\n\n**Killing–Hopf.** A complete, simply connected Riemannian manifold of constant curvature $K$ is isometric to exactly one of\n\n| $K$ | model | Stage 2 |\n|---|---|---|\n| $K > 0$ | $S^n(1/\\sqrt K)$ | 2.07 |\n| $K = 0$ | $\\mathbb{E}^n$ | 1.01–1.07 |\n| $K < 0$ | $H^n(1/\\sqrt{-K})$ | 2.06 |\n\nEvery other constant-curvature manifold — every **space form** — is a quotient $\\tilde M/\\Gamma$ by a discrete group of isometries acting freely and properly discontinuously. The geometry is fixed by $K$; the topology is a choice of $\\Gamma$.\n\n**Maximal symmetry.** The isometry group of an $n$-dimensional Riemannian manifold has dimension at most $\\tfrac12 n(n+1)$, and the three models are exactly the spaces attaining it. In dimension 2 that is 3, matching $E(2)$, $SO(3)$ and $PSL_2(\\mathbb R)$ — the three groups Stage 2 worked with. **This is where Erlangen and Riemann meet.** Klein starts from the group; Riemann starts from the metric; for constant curvature they determine each other.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "load(\"linearalgebra\")$\nratprint : false$\nts(e) := ratsimp(trigsimp(e))$\nchristoffel_hand(g, vars) := block([ginv, n_],\n  n_ : length(vars),  ginv : ratsimp(invert(g)),\n  makelist( makelist( makelist(\n    ts( sum( ginv[k][l]*( diff(g[j][l], vars[i])\n                        + diff(g[i][l], vars[j])\n                        - diff(g[i][j], vars[l]) ), l, 1, n_)/2 ),\n    j,1,n_), i,1,n_), k,1,n_) )$\nriem_hand(g, vars) := block([G, n_],\n  G : christoffel_hand(g, vars), n_ : length(vars),\n  makelist( makelist( makelist( makelist(\n    ts( diff(G[l][j][k], vars[i]) - diff(G[l][i][k], vars[j])\n        + sum( G[l][i][m]*G[m][j][k] - G[l][j][m]*G[m][i][k], m, 1, n_) ),\n    k,1,n_), j,1,n_), i,1,n_), l,1,n_) )$\nriem_low_hand(g, vars) := block([Rr, n_],\n  Rr : riem_hand(g, vars), n_ : length(vars),\n  makelist( makelist( makelist( makelist(\n    ts( sum( g[l][m]*Rr[m][i][j][k], m,1,n_) ),\n    l,1,n_), k,1,n_), j,1,n_), i,1,n_) )$\n\nassume(R0 > 0, u > 0, u < %pi, y > 0, ch > 0, ch < %pi, te > 0, te < %pi)$\n\n/* --- The constant-curvature form of the Riemann tensor --- */\n/* Our index order is Rm[i][j][k][l] = Rm_{ijkl} with the lowered index LAST\n   (4.04).  In that convention the model form reads\n      Rm_{ijkl} = K ( g_{il} g_{jk} − g_{ik} g_{jl} ),\n   which is the standard  K(g_ik g_jl − g_il g_jk)  with the last two\n   indices swapped.  We test both orderings and report which matches, rather\n   than asserting one. */\nmodel_form(g, K, sgn) := block([n_],\n  n_ : length(g),\n  makelist( makelist( makelist( makelist(\n    ratsimp( sgn*K*( g[i][k]*g[j][l] - g[i][l]*g[j][k] ) ),\n    l,1,n_), k,1,n_), j,1,n_), i,1,n_) )$\n\nmaxdev(A, B, n_) := block([m],\n  m : 0,\n  for i:1 thru n_ do for j:1 thru n_ do for k:1 thru n_ do for l:1 thru n_ do\n    if ts(A[i][j][k][l] - B[i][j][k][l]) # 0 then m : m + 1,\n  m )$\n\ncheck_form(g, vars, K, label) := block([Rm, n_],\n  Rm : riem_low_hand(g, vars), n_ : length(vars),\n  print(\"   \", label, \":  mismatches with +K(g_ik g_jl − g_il g_jk) = \",\n        maxdev(Rm, model_form(g, K, 1), n_),\n        \" ;  with −K(...) = \", maxdev(Rm, model_form(g, K, -1), n_)) )$\n\nprint(\"Rm_{ijkl} = ±K (g_ik g_jl − g_il g_jk)  —  which sign fits?\")$\ncheck_form(matrix([R0^2,0],[0,R0^2*sin(u)^2]), [u,v], 1/R0^2, \"S²(R₀)     \")$\ncheck_form(matrix([1/y^2,0],[0,1/y^2]),        [x,y], -1,     \"H²         \")$\ncheck_form(matrix([1,0],[0,rr^2]),             [rr,th], 0,    \"E² (polar) \")$\ncheck_form(matrix([1,0,0],[0,sin(ch)^2,0],[0,0,sin(ch)^2*sin(te)^2]),\n           [ch,te,ph], 1, \"S³(1)      \")$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"Zero mismatches in the −K column throughout: with the lowered index\")$\nprint(\"in the LAST slot the model form carries a minus sign relative to the\")$\nprint(\"textbook statement, which places it FIRST.  Same tensor, same K —\")$\nprint(\"only the index convention differs.  (4.04 recorded the same trap.)\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 5,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Rm_{ijkl} = ±K (g_ik g_jl − g_il g_jk)  —  which sign fits?\n    S²(R₀)      :  mismatches with +K(g_ik g_jl − g_il g_jk) =  4\n    ;  with −K(...) =  0\n    H²          :  mismatches with +K(g_ik g_jl − g_il g_jk) =  4\n    ;  with −K(...) =  0\n    E² (polar)  :  mismatches with +K(g_ik g_jl − g_il g_jk) =  0\n    ;  with −K(...) =  0\n    S³(1)       :  mismatches with +K(g_ik g_jl − g_il g_jk) =  12\n    ;  with −K(...) =  0\nZero mismatches in the −K column throughout: with the lowered index\nin the LAST slot the model form carries a minus sign relative to the\ntextbook statement, which places it FIRST.  Same tensor, same K —\nonly the index convention differs.  (4.04 recorded the same trap.)"
