          "text": [
            "EUCLIDEAN PLANE, g = dx² + dy²\n   X =  [1,0]    L_X g =  matrix([0,0],[0,0])\n   X =  [0,1]    L_X g =  matrix([0,0],[0,0])\n   X =  [-y,x]    L_X g =  matrix([0,0],[0,0])\n   two translations and one rotation: dim Isom = 3 = ½n(n+1) ✓\n   that is E(2), the group of 1.02–1.04.\nUNIT SPHERE, g = du² + sin²u dv²   (u polar, v azimuthal)\n   X =  [0,1]\n      L_X g =  matrix([0,0],[0,0])\n   X =  [sin(v),(cos(u)*cos(v))/sin(u)]\n      L_X g =  matrix([0,0],[0,0])\n   X =  [cos(v),-((cos(u)*sin(v))/sin(u))]\n      L_X g =  matrix([0,0],[0,0])\n   the three rotations about the coordinate axes: dim = 3 ✓\n   that is SO(3), the group of 2.07.\nHYPERBOLIC HALF-PLANE, g = (dx² + dy²)/y²\n   X =  [1,0]    L_X g =  matrix([0,0],[0,0])\n   X =  [x,y]    L_X g =  matrix([0,0],[0,0])\n   X =  [x^2-y^2,2*x*y]    L_X g =  matrix([0,0],[0,0])\n   translation, dilation, special conformal: dim = 3 ✓\n   these are the generators of PSL₂(ℝ), the group of 2.06.\n   In the complex coordinate z = x + iy the three fields are\n   1, z and z², whose flows are z ↦ z+t, z ↦ e^t z and\n   z ↦ z/(1−tz) — Möbius transformations, which is exactly what\n   2.06 obtained from circle geometry with no metric in sight.\nA SURFACE THAT IS NOT A SPACE FORM: torus of revolution\n   X =  [0,1]    L_X g =  matrix([0,0],[0,0])    (rotation ✓)\n   X =  [1,0]    L_X g =  matrix([0,0],[0,(-(2*cos(u))-4)*sin(u)])\n      not Killing — the offending entry is ∂_u(f²) ≠ 0.\n   Its curvature is non-constant (4.06), so dim Isom < 3.  Maximal\n   symmetry and constant curvature are the same condition."
